<div class="post-body">
    <h2>Studio Diary: Crafting Analog Atmospheres</h2>
    <p>
        Recorded in an analog home studio in Berlin, <em>"Midnight Dreams"</em> combines the unmistakable texture of vintage Roland synthesizer circuitry with lush tape delay loops. Alex Parker spent four weeks dialing in the bass sequence on an original 1982 Roland Juno-60 before tracking real electric bass guitar to ground the groove.
    </p>

    <blockquote>
        "There is a warmth to magnetic tape saturation that modern plugins approximate, but the tactile feel of turning physical knobs and hearing analog filters open up can never be replicated."
        <br><br><strong>— Alex Parker</strong>
    </blockquote>

